<v SPEAKER_3>Sure. I was in elementary school in the early 60s. And I'm not even sure how the interest began, but when especially talk about Project Blue Book came out, other kinds of things, I read whatever capacity I could. I had a couple of dreams that may have been influenced by sci-fi movies, although I don't know how many of those were around. In fact, it was kind of a recurring dream that it was almost like the initial scenario of an abduction, but it would stop right after I'd be lying in bed, which my regular bed and my brother was in a double bed with me. And I'm lying there, there's a big window by the bed, and all of a sudden this kind of blue-green light would come down from the sky through the window and hit me and freeze me. I couldn't move. My brother remained asleep. And then the dream would always end there. So my guess is, you know, by that time, excuse me, it's probably early 60s sometime. Maybe I'd seen some movies with that kind of thing, and that's why. But it certainly helped to encourage my interest. The other thing is that when I was a teenager, I would have been senior of high school, so I would have been 17 with a couple of buddies. I grew up in Savannah, Georgia. That's where I was born. And they have islands on the coast there, Tybee Islands, the nearest to Savannah has the beaches. One evening in the summer, walking along with them on the beach. And all of a sudden, we looked up and there were two huge, what were to us, unidentified anomalous figures. They didn't look so much like craft. They looked almost like what we might describe as circular plasma. Two of them that were white but with red and green lights inside of them. And to this day, they could have been, there may be some prosaic explanation for that. I don't know. But we got scared, jumped in the car, drove back to my home about eight miles away. It seemed to follow us to the sky, maybe not disappeared. But all these things, I'm just saying, whatever they actually were, certainly continued to increase my interest. And I've never lost it.

02:25:15.060 --> 02:25:27.400
<v SPEAKER_2>Which is wonderful. And I wonder, was there any, how intense was your religious, or your religion, or your faith when you were a child? And did those kind of counteract each other at all?

